SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
UID:260415vNC8FTVjh063efWQtXwkOw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T193000
UID:260415uDJFruWj5kSTu0Jb1Eaipw
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SRJC Fashion Studies Fashion Show "The Equinox"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T203000
UID:260412vfT0b2Y6Q0Kd6pWp517z0w
DESCRIPTION:SRJC fashion program is proud to announce the annual student r
 un fashion show\, “The Equinox”.  The show will be held on Thursday\,
  April 30th\, 2026\,  SRJC Petaluma Campus Clocktower Plaza. This year’
 s students are ecstatic to reveal that this year’s show will be unique i
 n its production and scope. “We’re taking lighting and aesthetic immer
 sion to a whole new level\,” states the venue organizer\, Sebastian Faiv
 re. Show director\, Valeria Silva\, claims\, “This year's theme is so in
 teresting and different\, and I feel so excited to be working with so many
  creative individuals who are putting a lot into the show\, so it's defini
 tely going to be a must go!”\n\nThis year’s theme is The Equinox *\\-*
  the change of seasons\, the shift from dark winter to bright spring. The 
 equinox is representative of two opposites\, not in conflict\, but standin
 g together in harmony. Hope and rebellion\, night and day\, darkness and r
 adiant color. The goal of the show is to celebrate a range of creative sty
 les that represent people\, with styles ranging from bubbly and poppy to d
 ark and alternative. \n\nThe show will feature the “Black and White” 
 contest\, where students are prompted to design a look by only using speci
 fic black and white fabrics. Audience members will even be able to vote on
  their favorite look from the competition. The core show will consist of t
 wo acts\, one representing darkness and one representing light. There will
  also be a series of collections made from student designers\, who are all
  excited to showcase their vision\, hard work and techniques learned in fa
 shion studies. \n\nGeneral admission is $20\, and SRJC students are $10. 
 Tickets are available on Eventbrite.  Doors open at 7 PM\, with the show 
 beginning at 7:30. More information is available at the SRJC Fashion Studi
 es Website.
LOCATION:SRJC Petaluma Campus
URL:https://fashion.santarosa.edu/event/spring-2026-fashion-show
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
