UID:2604189H96qGHT6kO1NMHdOa6cHg
DESCRIPTION:STELLA HEATH & THE BILLIE HOLIDAY PROJECT – ALBUM RELEASE TO
 UR May 1st\, 2026 7:30 PM Tickets: $35 Tables   $25 Balcony The Billie Hol
 iday Project is a captivating live concert experience that brings the musi
 c and story of Billie Holiday to life through powerful performances and ri
 ch historical context. Led by vocalist Stella Heath\, the show weaves toge
 ther iconic songs with storytelling that illuminates Holiday’s artistry\
 , resilience\, and enduring influence. Featuring a stellar ensemble\, the 
 performance offers an intimate and engaging journey through one of jazz’
 s most influential voices. Presented as part of the For Billie album relea
 se tour\, this special concert celebrates the legacy of Billie Holiday whi
 le connecting her music to audiences today.” Soper Reese Theatre Members
 hips discounts will apply
LOCATION:Soper-Reese Theatre
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2141746783284867/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BFA Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T160000
UID:260417KYQNNHUoskG8Cf60X7jkMg
DESCRIPTION:Each spring\, the University Art Gallery proudly presents the 
 Bachelor of Fine Arts \\(BFA\\) Exhibition\, showcasing the work of Sonoma
  State University's graduating BFA class. The 2026 BFA Exhibition will be 
 on view April 23-May 23\, 2026. Offered by SSU's Art Department\, the BFA 
 degree is distinguished from the BA by its rigorous\, studio-intensive cur
 riculum. The program requires an additional year of focused study\, includ
 ing advanced coursework in studio art\, art history\, and art theory. Ofte
 n regarded as the degree of choice for students pursuing graduate or profe
 ssional studies\, the BFA fosters significant artistic development within 
 a concentrated creative environment. For both students and faculty\, this 
 exhibition represents a culminating achievement-an opportunity to present 
 a carefully curated selection of each artist's strongest work in a profess
 ional gallery setting\, exhibited alongside their peers. Opening Reception
 : Thursday\, April 23\, 2026 4:00-6:00 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/bfa-exhibition/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
