BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love & Information at Napa Valley College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T200000
UID:260424WLk4Kahw502xmdPkHzVzug
DESCRIPTION:Written by Caryl Churchill\, this play explores the complexiti
 es of human connection in the information age. The story delves into them
 es of love\, knowledge\, and identity\, presenting a kaleidoscope of conte
 mporary human experiences. In a world saturated with texts\, headlines\, 
 data\, and digital noise\, Churchill’s daring work asks a simple but urg
 ent question: how do we truly connect? \n\nChurchill's sharp dialogue and
  minimalist style create a sense of urgency\, prompting audiences to refle
 ct on how they process information and form connections in an increasingly
  digital world. \n\nDirected by Olivia Cowell & Jennifer King.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/love-information/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love & Information
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T200000
UID:260424DT-O_Ujd5Eyv_Eq5C7Jcpg
DESCRIPTION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center \\(PAC\\) presents 
 Love & Information\, the electrifying contemporary play by celebrated play
 wright Caryl Churchill. In a world saturated with texts\, headlines\, dat
 a\, and digital noise\, Churchill’s daring work asks a simple but urgent
  question: how do we truly connect? \n\nFast-moving\, surprising\, and de
 eply human\, Love & Information unfolds through a kaleidoscope of short\, 
 vivid scenes. Moments of intimacy collide with flashes of humor\, anxiety\
 , curiosity\, and longing as characters search for meaning in an age of 
 constant communication. A confession\, a secret\, a scientific discovery\,
  a memory—each scene reveals how love\, knowledge\, and identity shape o
 ur lives. \n\nChurchill’s razor-sharp writing invites audiences to piec
 e together the story themselves\, discovering connections between moments 
 that are by turns funny\, unsettling\, tender\, and profound. The result i
 s a theatrical experience that mirrors the rhythm of modern life—fragmen
 ted\, immediate\, and emotionally resonant. \n\n“Love & Information ca
 ptures the speed and complexity of contemporary life while revealing the d
 eep human longing for connection beneath it\,” said co-directors Jenni
 fer King and Olivia Cowell. “The play challenges actors to move quickly 
 between characters\, ideas\, and emotional worlds\, and our student ensemb
 le embraces that challenge with imagination and precision.” \n\nThe pro
 duction is co-directed by Jennifer King\, Napa Valley College Theater Arts
  Department Coordinator/Artistic Director and professional stage director\
 , and Olivia Cowell\, Napa Valley College Theater and Film Studies Instruc
 tor and Executive Director of Cafeteria Kids Theater. Both are leaders of 
 Shakespeare Napa Valley and bring a shared commitment to dynamic ensemble 
 storytelling to the production. \n\nLove & Information will be performed 
 in the intimate Studio Theater of the Napa Valley College Performing Arts 
 Center\, placing audiences just steps away from the actors and immersing t
 hem in the immediacy of Churchill’s theatrical world. With only six perf
 ormances\, seating is limited and audiences are encouraged to secure tic
 kets early by visiting www.performingartnapavalley. \n\nInventive\, prov
 ocative\, and surprisingly moving\, Love & Information showcases the ver
 satility of Napa Valley College’s student performers while inviting audi
 ences to reflect on how we communicate\, what we know\, and what it truly 
 means to connect. \n\nPerformances:  April 24\, 2026 7:00 pm  April 2
 5\, 2026 7:00 pm  April 26\, 2026 2:00 pm  May 1\, 2026 7:00 pm  
 May 2\, 2026 7:00 pm  May 3\, 2026 2:00 pm \n\nLocation:  Napa Vall
 ey College Performing Arts Center\, Main Theater  2277 Napa Vallejo Hwy 
  Napa\, CA 94558 \n\nTickets & Information:  https://performingartsnapav
 alley.org/love-information/
LOCATION:Napa Valley College
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/love-information/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
