BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Garagiste Wine Festival: 8th Annual Northern Exposure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T170000
UID:260422e_AvYXW58EW4ERG3m82gkw
DESCRIPTION:The 8th Annual Garagiste Festival: Northern Exposure is coming
  back on May 2\, 2026 to give you rare access to the region's best small\,
  hard-to-find winemakers. At this intimate event\, you will discover and t
 aste amazing\, cutting edge wines from over 40 high-quality\, micro-produc
 tion\, commercial wineries from Napa\, Sonoma\, Mendocino\, Sierra Foothil
 ls\, and more.\n\nFind out for yourself why we’ve been selling out our e
 vents for ten years and why we were named the \\#1 Wine Festival in the Co
 untry by USA Today! Meet the winemakers and hear directly from them about 
 the ins and outs of their winemaking styles.\n\nOver 90% of Garagiste wine
 ries do not have a tasting room\, so this is truly a singular chance to di
 scover and meet the next great winemakers and get the opportunity to taste
  their amazing micro-production wines. Your appointment to try these wine
 s is all in one room\, right here! You won't be able to duplicate this tas
 ting experience at any other wine event.  \n\nMeet the winemakers\, tast
 e their passion!\n\n2026 Winemaker Participants include: Amalgam Wines\, 
 Burning Bench Cellars\, Carpenter Wine\, Cazadero Winery\, Chaney Family W
 inery\, Cormorant Cellars\, Crosby Roamann\, Flora Ranch Co.\, Forgotten U
 nion Wines\, G & C Lurton Estate\, Gothic Noir Wine\, Greyscale Wines\, Ja
 mbe de Bois Wines Kendric Vineyards\, Krueger Vaught\, Lussier Wine Co.\, 
 Maybach Family Cellars\, McCarter Cellars\, Mersenne Wines\, Mon Premier W
 ines\, Oceano Wines\, Oxlee Graham Wines\, Panther Ridge Vineyards\, Pine 
 Mountain Vineyards\, Puccioni Vineyards\, Rock & Clay Wines\, Shick Family
  Wines\, Spur Road Wines\, Staysail Cellars\, and Y.B. Wine Co.\n\n GRAND
  TASTING: 2:00-5:00pm - Includes unlimited tasting with over 30 small lot 
 winemakers\, complimentary cheese\, bread and charcuterie\, as well as sam
 ples from local artisan vendors.\n\nRARE & RESERVE EARLY ACCESS: 1:00-5:00
 pm  \n\nEntry an hour early at 1:00pm and enjoy access to Rare & Reserve 
 wines only being poured during this hour. Limited tickets available to cre
 ate a less crowded experience. Only 150 Tickets are available to this ses
 sion.
LOCATION:Sonoma Vets Building
URL:https://www.garagistefestival.com/sonoma-may-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
