BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening Reception: Perfectly Imperfect by Cameron Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T200000
UID:260422F_DCggNxJEiw5BNha9egfg
DESCRIPTION:Perfectly Imperfect\n\nBy Featured Artist Cameron Story at Ush
 er Gallery\n\nThis exhibition focuses on the power of imperfection.\n\nJoi
 n us for the opening reception of Perfectly Imperfect on May 2nd from 5pm 
 to 8pm. Enjoy live music by The Hot Clams\, a spread of refreshments and w
 ine\, and our lively community! Perfectly Imperfect will be on display at 
 Usher Gallery from April 28th to May 31st.\n\n“The concept of perfection
  can drive us or paralyze us\, but either way\, we are trying to live up t
 o something that doesn’t truly exist. The fear of not achieving perfecti
 on often stops us before we even begin. Think about how often you’ve all
 owed this idea to intercept your desire to try something new or express yo
 urself differently for fear of judgment. I felt the desire to paint for ye
 ars before ever putting paint to canvas. Now\, through acrylic\, resin\, m
 etal leaf\, and a variety of mixed media\, I’m able to push past these f
 ears and express my most authentic self\, fully embracing that it will not
  be perfect. Nor would I want it to be. If creativity is to flow freely\, 
 it needs to be imperfect. This has allowed me to become an artist\, and I
 ’m truly grateful. Whether it’s art or any other driving force in our 
 lives\, I encourage everyone to consider imperfection as a gift that allow
 s us to grow and thrive.”\n\nCameron Story\, Show Statement
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
URL:https://ushergallerypetaluma.com/blogs/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eco-Wise Workshop Series: Beyond The Lawn
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T120000
UID:260420ClCrLtw3n0OH4gYWoTPm9A
DESCRIPTION:Don't let drought\, muddy lawns\, and crumbling creek beds cra
 mp your style! Tour the Native Plant Garden\, Copeland Creek corridor\, an
 d see the new bioswale at the Agroecology Garden at SSU. Learn tips for na
 tive and low-water landscaping for your own home from two forward-thinking
  SSU students working on projects with the Center for Environmental Inquir
 y and Plant Futures Club. Explore options for replacing your lawn with nat
 ive plants to create habitat corridors and prevent erosion\, reduce water 
 use and deal with puddling\, and support local ecosystems while decreasing
  maintenance needs. \n\nParticipants will watch a planting demo then have
  the opportunity to take home a free native bunchgrass ready to plant! Lig
 ht refreshments provided.\n\n*This event is part of The City of Cotati and
  City of Rohnert Park's Eco-Wise Workshop Series\, designed to inspire su
 stainability for everyday life. Through interactive activities\, local exp
 ertise\, and community-driven solutions\, the Eco-Wise Workshop Series bri
 ngs residents together to explore simple steps that make a big environment
 al impact. Check out other offerings each month from February through Octo
 ber 2026.*
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://www.cotaticity.gov/1690/Eco-Wise-Workshop-Series-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
