BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bay Area Playback Theater "Exploring Stories of Relationships"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T210000
UID:260314rE2S_yoM60ufXwVcVBj5nQ
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday May 2\, 2026 at 7:00pm the San Geronimo Valley C
 ommunity Center welcomes back Bay Area Playback Theater "Exploring Stories
  of Relationships".\n\nThrough the transformative lens of Playback Theater
 \, Deep Improv Theater\, actors and musicians will bring your true experie
 nces to life using movement music\, metaphor and spoken word.\n\nRelations
 hips are vital to our lives\; every life is woven from them.  They are f
 un\, difficult\, amazing\, inspiring\, satisfying\, and/or challenging. W
 e have people we love\, avoid\, and put up with. We have them with animal
 s\, objects\, places\, ideas\, money\, and society. What relationships sh
 aped you\, elated you\, irritated you\, pushed you\, made you grow\, laugh
  and/or cry?\n\n No two shows are alike. Come as you are\, tell your sto
 ry or simply watch them come to life on stage.\n\n BayAreaPlayback.com
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sgvperformingarts.eventcalendarapp.com/bay-area-playback-theat
 er-exploring-stories-of-releationships
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GUIDE DOGS FOR THE BLIND'S GRADUATION CEREMONIES MELT HEARTS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T143000
UID:260314bQ_nppKzBkS-t8hNDynXIA
DESCRIPTION:Guide Dogs for the Blind \\(GDB\\) will celebrate its guide d
 og team graduates every other Saturday with public graduation ceremonies a
 t the organization’s campus in San Rafael. These touching public events 
 have inspired tears in even the most stoic audience members\, as graduatin
 g guide dog teams proudly take the stage. Families are welcome at the cere
 monies\, which honor the independence and companionship that GDB’s gui
 de dogs provide for GDB’s clients who are blind or visually impaired. T
 he events also allow GDB’s clients to meet the puppy raisers who cared 
 for their canine heroes prior to beginning formal training at GDB’s cam
 pus. Ceremonies also recognize recent graduates of GDB’s Orientation an
 d Mobility \\(O&M\\) Program\, K9 Buddy Program\, and Breeder Dog Program
 .\n\nAdmission is free\, and Kleenex will be provided. Pre-registered bus 
 groups are welcome. Public tours of the campus are offered on the days of 
 the ceremonies. Visit www.guidedogs.com for more information. Graduat
 ion events are also livestreamed at https://www.youtube.com/@gdb\\_offici
 al/streams.
LOCATION:Guide Dogs for the Blind
URL:https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
