BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What's the Buzz?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T163000
UID:260420mnmbOkEcZ0G_QBtUkueGkg
DESCRIPTION:Come join members of the Pacific Coast Entomological Society a
 s they hear from student researchers and traverse the nine plant communiti
 es of Osborn Preserve to search for spectacular insects! These animals are
  more fascinating and important than most people understand: they play vit
 al roles in ecosystems\, including pollination\, decomposition\, and servi
 ng as food for other animals\, communicate through pheromones\, sounds\, a
 nd even light. And though we hear most about harmful insects such as crop 
 pests and those that carry human diseases\, many are beneficial in ways w
 e wouldn't know how to live without.
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/buzz
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cotati Community Mural Paint Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T130000
UID:260420dwWf6yt2I0ucApPdGqAiNg
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to announce that we will begin painting our fir
 st ever community mural in Cotati on Sunday\, April 19! We will be transfo
 rming the restroom building at the newly renovated Sunflower Park on East 
 Cotati Avenue into a beautiful four sided piece of art. We will be working
  with Cotati local artist Asherah Weiss.\n\nWe'd love to have our communit
 y join us for the three planned days we have scheduled so far. The first d
 ay\, 4/19\, will be priming only. The other days will be painting with mor
 e color.\n\nRainy days will be rescheduled.\n\nYou can RSVP online at: htt
 ps://bit.ly/cotatimural\n\nChildren welcome with adult supervision. No exp
 erience necessary and high schoolers are welcome to help for community ser
 vice hours.\n\nAll supplies and lunch will be provided! We hope to see you
  there!\n\nQuestions? Email awilson@cotaticity.gov or call 707-665-4222.
LOCATION:Sunflower Park
URL:https://bit.ly/cotatimural
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature's Wild Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T160000
UID:260418_xpFiQHwiEe4PJPFy4x89A
DESCRIPTION:Viewed from afar\, the hills of California appear as large swa
 ths of gold\, or green\, depending upon the season. In the spring\, howeve
 r\, other colors punctuate the landscape as the wildflowers stretch toward
  the warmth and the light. When you look even more closely\, dazzling deta
 ils become clear: the delicate intricacies of the grasses\, the patterns o
 f the wildflowers\, the hectic activity of the insects\, even the richness
  of the soil.\n\nJoin members of the California Native Plant Society’s \
 \(CNPS\\) local chapters on this exploration of the hills and valleys of t
 he Galbreath Wildlands Preserve in southern Mendocino County. While we wil
 l not cover the full 3\,670-acre preserve\, we will drive through much of 
 it\, stopping to enjoy the diversity of wildflowers and other native plant
 s that grow on the hillsides and in the dales.
LOCATION:Galbreath Wildlands Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/natures-wild-garden
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
