BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Experiment Farm Open House and Plant Sale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
UID:260412BM-J0JmUGUicMJmn5J5puQ
DESCRIPTION:The Luther Burbank Experiment Farm welcomes you to stop and ex
 plore our historic farm and cottage during Farm Trail's Spring Tour on Sun
 day\, May 3rd from 10AM to 3PM. Free and family friendly!\n\nLuther Burban
 k \\(1849-1926\\) was a pioneering botanist who developed more than 800 va
 rieties of plants\, including the Shasta daisy\, Santa Rosa plum\, freesto
 ne peach\, and the Burbank russet potato - used in 70% of the US's process
 ed potato dishes like french fries.\n\nVisit his experimental farm in Seba
 stopol\, where he did most of his work\, and see his plants come to life! 
 Volunteers maintain this 3 acre plot\, complete with orchard\, demonstrati
 on garden\, and plant nursery where we still grow plants for sale. His cot
 tage is beautifully preserved and will be open to the public for this rare
  occasion.\n\nThere will be heirloom fruit trees and perennial plants for 
 sale\, including many of Burbank's finest. Kids activities and a craft sal
 e with local artists on feature. See the farm at the height of bloom - the
  Shasta daisies and more will be in full show! Enjoy a picnic at our table
 s\, explore the self-guided tour\, and find fun local gifts at the Luther 
 Burbank Experiment Farm!
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Experiment Farm
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/25790681533942602/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taylor Trades Outdoor Market - May 3
