BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Bikefest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
UID:260331x5YMgYhayEKOSxTLInI6KQ
DESCRIPTION:Get stoked for Napa Bikefest 2026! \n\n​Presented by the Na
 pa County Bicycle Coalition\, Napa Valley Transportation Authority\, and P
 G&E\, Napa Bikefest is a free day-long family-friendly community celebrati
 on of all things bike. The event brings together bike enthusiasts from acr
 oss the Bay Area to celebrate life on two wheels and to help those who are
  new to riding get started. Learn more at www.napabikefest.org! \n\n​Bi
 kefest festivities include: \n\n\\- the North Bay's largest bike swap m
 eet where you can get a great deal on new and used bikes\, parts\, and ac
 cessories \n\n\\- awesome music by the Napa High Jazz Band and DJ Rotten 
 Robbie \n\n\\- a kids bike rodeo & Passport to Bikefest program\, thr
 ough which kids can win awesome prizes! \n\n\\- great food\, beer and w
 ine offerings \n\n\\- community and bike industry booths \n\n\\- bike co
 ntests and games for all ages - with prizes! \n\n\\- Ask-A-Bike Mechanic 
 booth \n\n\\- Stretching for Bicyclists led by Julia Salvador\, DPT of Am
 erican Canyon Bike Shop \n\n\\- bike & helmet decorating station \n\n\\-
  free group bike rides\, the Kidical Mass Ride and two pace group option
 s for the Vine Trail Month of Movement Ride \n\n​Admission is free\, ev
 ent runs 9:00am–3:00pm in NEW LOCATION Oxbow Commons Park on McKinstry S
 treet in Napa. Easily accessible from the Napa Valley Vine Trail and River
  Trail. \n\n​See www.napabikefest.org for more info - details are being
  published as they are confirmed\, so keep checking back for updates! See 
 you there!
LOCATION:Oxbow Commons Park
URL:http://www.napabikefest.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:260330y-PYB1GQI0CRPmEYzLFR4Q
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
