BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:53rd Annual Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:260316Uf9PYE0m2EewWTljPT-Lag
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 53rd Annual Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival.\n
 \nDates: May 2nd &amp\; 3rd 2026\n\n10AM-5PM\n\nTheme: FISH TO DISH\n\nWel
 come to the Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival\, a family friendly fundraiser
  for 25 local nonprofits. Since 1973\, this event has celebrated our local
  fisherman and it's when salmon season is kicked off with a blessing of th
 e fleet. The Festival is packed with events for people of all ages: over 6
 0 craft booths\, live music\, good food\, entertainment and more.\n\nThe F
 isherman's Festival is an all-volunteer event\, and proceeds benefit Bodeg
 a Bay Area community services.\n\n \n\nThe festival has its origin as a ce
 lebration of the start of the Salmon fishing season and the annual Blessin
 g of the Fleet. Each year's theme is chosen by the Bodega Bay Fisherman's 
 Marketing Association. At the Festival site itself\, you'll see a wooden b
 oat challenge where participating teams build a vessel and compete in a bo
 at race.  Sign up today https://www.bbfishfest.org/wooden-boat-challenge/\
 \#register\n\n \n\nA favorite attraction is the wine booth featuring more 
 than 25 Sonoma County wines and a beer booth with several local ales. Plus
  we have something for every palate\; barbecued oysters\, local fish &amp\
 ; chips\, clam chowder and a variety of non-seafood food trucks. Live musi
 c and entertainers perform on the main stage all day Saturday and Sunday. 
 Artisans and vendors from all over California and beyond offer a wide sele
 ction of arts and crafts.\n\n \n\nThe Fisherman's Festival is a great venu
 e for kids with a play area for face painting\, games\, a touch tank tide 
 pool\, jumpy houses\, pony rides. Leashed Pets are welcome and encouraged 
 to attend. Sunday morning will feature the Blessing of the Fishing Fleet w
 hen decorated boats parade out of the harbor to receive a blessing from lo
 cal clergy.\n\n \n\nLive Music All day on main stage\n\nSaturday May 2\n\n
 10am-11:30am The Rotten Tomatoes Rock Band\n\nNoon-2pm Dry Creek Station C
 ountry Band\n\n3pm-5pm Tainted Love- Best of the 80's Live\n\nSunday May 3
 \n\n10:30-Noon 40 Fathom's\n\n12:30 PM-2:15pm Petty Rocks - Tom Petty Cove
 r Band\n\n3PM-5PM Mustache Harbor\n\nVisit www.bbfishfest.org for more det
 ails\n\nParking Map \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n 
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/53rd-annual-bodega-bay-fis
 hermans-festival?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: The Poetic Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T180000
UID:260314vfK_QenW8k65Vxqa0culEQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  3/13/26\n\n**APRIL EXHIBIT: THE 
 POETIC LANDSCAPE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  March 30  – April 26\, 2026\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, APRIL 4\, 2026\, 3-5 pm: Join us to meet KAREN MILL
 ER and PHYLLIS RAPP\;  celebrate the show and enjoy a poetry reading by f
 eatured guest\, Linda Loveland Reid\, gallery artist and published author.
   Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Karen Miller\,** presents **The Poetic Landscape\,** pa
 stel paintings that convey Miller’s personal experience in connecting wi
 th the intrinsic beauty of natural places. In these pieces\, color\, fluid
  shapes and rhythmic design combine to create an uplifting mood – a true
  poetic interlude.  Evoking a happy mood\, “Geyserville Sunflowers\,”
  turning to the sun by nature\, joyfully dance in its luminescence. By the
  river’s edge\, concentric reflections conjure a calm sense of wellbeing
  in “Fetch.”  The viewer feels welcomed by a warm embrace entering a 
 shaded secret spot in “September Trellis.”  Focused on local scenes\,
  these works truly hone in on the stunning landscape out our doors.  Mill
 er remarked “ As I contemplate the very real places of beauty surroundin
 g us\, I try to express my painterly response in hopes it will engender re
 cognition by the viewers.” \n\nMeet the artist: Miller will be hosting 
 the Gallery on March 30\, April 5 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n The Stai
 rway Smallworks Showcase features **Phyllis Rapp’s Magic Moments\,** a c
 ollection of watercolors that create an atmosphere that is both introspect
 ive and magical.  Familiar domestic scenes are transformed as humans inte
 ract with animals and birds in floral settings.  In “Silent Watcher” 
 the red-headed young woman’s green eyes lock onto ours as she stares ahe
 ad\, flanked by her avian companion.  Experiencing these works is a like 
 taking a mini-step on the wild side\, an exciting and fun experience.\n\nM
 eet the artist: Rapp will be hosting the Gallery on March 30 and April 10 
 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\
 , April 2\, 5 – 6 pm.  The theme for the 2026 kickoff event is Bouquets
  to Art.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is
  a community event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries p
 articipating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Cente
 r Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 
 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Con
 tact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
