BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Stick Loom Weaving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T173000
UID:2602285fBzS4hTn021mF-Vt7qUSw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, March 21\, 2026 2:00 – 3:30 PM\n\nLoc
 ation\n\nRoom 110\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nFamily\, Kids\n\nAg
 e\\(s\\)\n\n7-12\n\nAll children must be accompanied by an adult to attend
 .\n\n$30 – Per Family\, max of 3 people. Learn ancient stick loom weavin
 g in this hands-on class. Create a beautiful tapestry using natural materi
 als\, simple techniques\, and your choice of colors.\n\nAbout the Class\n\
 nCome learn the ancient craft of weaving with a stick loom! In this family
 -friendly class\, you’ll learn to hand-weave a simple tapestry using sti
 cks as your loom. The demonstration will include setting up the warp threa
 ds\, learning a simple over-under stitch pattern and the final knot step. 
 There will be a variety of stick shapes to choose from and plenty of room 
 to play with pattern and color. And voila! You’ll leave the class with y
 our stick-loom tapestry \\(either in progress or completed\, depending on 
 the chosen scale\\). Hang your weaving on your wall to bring nature indoor
 s or from a tree to bring your artistry outside! This class is open to par
 ents with their children ages 7 through 12.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/family-stick-loom-weaving/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:verygently & Kameron Marlowe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T000000
UID:2602245mrVMF591UaiaH3DLl8B9w
DESCRIPTION:verygently is the collective force of three established Nashvi
 lle singer-songwriters—Drew Erwin\, Joey Hendricks\, and Tristan Bushman
 —who came together in early 2024. With tours alongside Augustana\, The B
 and Camino\, and The Fray\, combined with their debut EP\, the band quickl
 y turned heads thanks to their high-energy live shows and songs that blend
  wit and vulnerability\, weaving heartache with the undeniable charm of th
 ree best friends sharing the stage.\n\nTheir recently released EP\, ‘FAM
 E!’\, produced by Noah Gundersen\, marks a confident evolution for the b
 and. Combining Bushman’s moody storytelling\, Erwin’s soaring melodies
 \, and Hendricks’ ‘70s-infused songwriting\, the record feels both fre
 sh and nostalgic. Recorded to analog tape at the legendary FAME Studios in
  Muscle Shoals\, Alabama\, ‘FAME!’ solidifies verygently as a band who
 se collaborative collective artistry is greater than the sum of its parts
 —setting the stage for an exciting future.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107934949?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
