BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T203000
UID:260426YQF6Y3fLlEuMKa7wiW6quw
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nMay 7- May 28\n\nThis is a beginner cuban salsa—you will l
 earn your basic footwork and turns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the 
 fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, including body movement\, rhythm\, musicalit
 y\, footwork\, partner connection\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by a
 uthentic Cuban dance culture.\n\nWe focus on proper technique\, coordinati
 on\, flow\, and natural body expression\, while also building confidence a
 nd strong foundations.\n\nClasses are structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and 
 body movement\n\n• Footwork and rhythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork tech
 nique\n\n• Short combinations and practical applications\n\nOur goal is 
 to help you understand how to dance salsa\, not just memorize steps — de
 veloping timing\, connection\, and a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\
 n\nCome dance with us\, grow your technique\, and experience the energy an
 d flavor of Cuba in a supportive and welcoming environment.\n\nBook your s
 pot\n\nDate & Time: 4week class\, May 7- May 28\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\n
 Address: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minu
 tes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T170000
UID:260424sJr1XioGKEu1Pl4mpjEoqA
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Album Tour: Back pOrchEstra at Jack London Lodge\, Glen Ellen\
 , Thu May 7
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T200000
UID:260424nEZIhzPfc0CGf3ZpJdgu-Q
DESCRIPTION:New American Roots Album Awareness Tour continues! Back pOrchE
 stra at Jack London Lodge and Saloon Concert Series\, Glen Ellen\, Thu May
  7\, 6-8 pm\n\nLucky to have such talented players... Candy Girard (played
  w/ Delaney Bramlet\, Tanya Tucker\, Jerry Garcia) on violin\, Tim Eschlim
 an (Etta James\, Commander Cody & His Western Airmen\, The Christmas Jug B
 and) on vocals & resonator guitar\, Bowen Brown (John Lee Hooker\, Tommy C
 astro) on drums\, Jen Rund (Lumination\, The Real Sarahs) on bass\, Gary P
 otterton (NRPS\, Texas Chainsaw) on guitar.\n\nFacebook event page: https:
 //www.facebook.com/events/1642368653696179\n\n13740 Arnold Drive Glen Elle
 n\, CA 95442 - (707) 938-8510\n\nA broad range of Indie Rock and Americana
  and the American Roots styles that inspired it: country blues\, Zydeco\, 
 roots rock\, Tex Mex\, rockabilly\, Singer-Songwriter\, Motown\, Brazilian
  and Louisiana music. This combo\, sprung out of the pandemic has develope
 d a unique\, catchy\, funky\, moody sound\, drawing from the varied past. 
 Comparison's have been made to the music of Big Al Anderson (NRBQ)\, The B
 and\, JJ Cale\, Asleep At The Wheel\, Dan Hicks\, Buddy & Julie Miller\, J
 esse Ed Davis & Levon Helm.\n\nJack London Saloon: Experience quintessenti
 al Glen Ellen like the locals do. Steeped in turn of the century history a
 nd charm\, The Jack London Saloon offers a spacious and beautiful Creeksid
 e Patio... savor the serene setting beside the Sonoma Creek. Experience a 
 vintage landmark among Sonoma Wine Country restaurants. The Saloon feature
 s wine country comfort food and the best burger in Sonoma. The beverage li
 st highlights an incredible variety of Wine Country vintages\, craft beers
 \, and cocktails.\n\n"...The guitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin t
 races lines that oscillate between melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm 
 section moves forward with a tranquil groove that never rushes but never f
 alters... Back pOrchEstra delivers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human 
 record. An album that makes you want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\
 , and let the stories do their work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine (trans
 lated from French) https://www.zicazic.com/zicazine/index.php?option=conte
 nt&task=view&id=18836\n\n"...What sets 'Stories In The Heart' apart is its
  sense of balance. Resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\,
  dobro\, and Telecaster create a flexible\, roots-forward palette that all
 ows Back Porchestra to move between styles fluidly. The songs echo traditi
 ons without reenacting them\, keeping one foot in the past and the other f
 irmly planted in the present." - Vince's Hot Picks (Best of 2026) New Rele
 ases Now\n\nsee our music video\, "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu
 .be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hint
 s of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nOur "Voices In My Head (Genre Whip
 lash)" made the Top 100 Albums at Alt.Country Specialty Chart.\n\nChoose y
 our music service: https://orcd.co/dw640r4\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-Music Ca
 rds available all over\, including https://www.globerecords.com\n\n"It's o
 ne fine album" - Ben Fong-Torres (Rolling Stone\, Almost Famous)\n\n"...ev
 okes artists from multiple decades over the last century and embraces ever
 ything from indie-rock and Americana to Celtic\, Motown\, and Western swin
 g. If you need a reference point\, look to bands like Dan Hicks and His Ho
 t Licks and Asleep at the Wheel\, whose records also draw on disparate sou
 rces." - Jeff Burger\, Americana Highway\n\nsee!:\n\nhttp://www.BackPorchE
 stra.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c
 0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra\n\nhttps://
 www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/art
 ist/0s4VMCtb1EMddafnDPZDDM?si=cGVFpp1JROaDEvSrJpKVjA\n\n#rootsrock #americ
 anrootsmusic #americanamusic #rockabillymusic #twangyguitar #backporchestr
 a #acousticmusic
LOCATION:Jack London Lodge
URL:http://www.BackPorchEstra.com#cal
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
