BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kevin Gerzevitz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T000000
UID:260417ARFyIgB9skmULYwj4i96dw
DESCRIPTION:Kevin Gerzevitz is a professional musician\, composer and teac
 her based in the San Francisco Bay Area. He is a keyboardist\, specializin
 g in piano\, accordion and jazz organ\, and is often performing with The J
 ules Broussard New Orleans Jazz Band\, Vintage Jukebox Orchestra\, the B3B
 4 Organ Jazz Quartet\, as well as The Kevin Gerzevitz Trio. He has a BMA f
 rom the University of Michigan \\(1990\\)\, majoring in Music Theory and G
 erman\, an Orff-Schulwerk Teaching Certification from Mills College \\(200
 5\\)\, and is currently the Music & Movement specialist at Pacific Primary
  School in San Francisco. \n\n​\n\nKevin worked closely in the 90’s wi
 th music producer Mark Needham and talent agent Jeff Saltzman\, along with
  Michael Franti's guitarist Jason Bowman on a recording project called Mem
 ory.Man\, cultivating his songwriting skills and left hand synth bass chop
 s. He has shared the stage with José Feliciano\, Michael Manring\, James 
 Carter\, Sheldon Brown\, Todd Boston\, Silvia Nakkach\, Ed Sarath and Dave
  Liebman.
LOCATION:Arlene Francis Center for Spirit\, Art\, and Politics
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108216132?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
