BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Postcards - Spring 2026 Concert Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T210000
UID:260404gW26E9csrE2W5ec2ZW0a7w
DESCRIPTION:The Occidental Community Choir puts on live concerts featuring
  an eclectic mix of locally composed music\, classical and contemporary ch
 oral pieces\, poetry\, and spoken word from our community in the redwoods 
 of Northern California.\n\nThe Occidental Community Choir invites audience
 s to its Spring concert series\, Postcards\, a musical journey through mem
 ory\, connection\, and the moments that shape our lives.In times that can 
 feel uncertain or isolating\, even small gestures of connection—a postca
 rd\, a call\, a simple message saying “I’m thinking of you”—can re
 mind us that we are not alone. Postcards is built around that spirit of re
 aching out. Each piece in the program serves as a musical postcard: a snap
 shot from a particular time and place\, carrying stories of joy\, longing\
 , hope\, and reflection.\n\nSome of these musical postcards arrive bright 
 and sun-drenched\; others carry the weathered edges of memory. Together th
 ey form a collection of moments that remind us our lives are measured not 
 only in years\, but in the experiences that stay with us and the ones we s
 hare with others.Through song\, the choir becomes both sender and recipien
 t—offering voices as messages of care\, presence\, and connection. Postc
 ards is a reminder that even in difficult times\, music can help us reach 
 across distance and say something simple and powerful: you matter\, you ar
 e connected\, and you are not alone.\n\nJoin the Occidental Community Choi
 r this spring for an evening of music that carries stories\, memories\, an
 d hope into a weary and waiting world.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center For the Arts
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/postcards-spring-2026-c
 oncert-series/18501377/2026-05-09T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Native Arts Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T160000
UID:260401wRY3wuQHPEy8i643_M6ILw
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to The Progressive Tribal Alliance Our Native Arts Fes
 tival is a vibrant celebration of Native art\, artists\, and community. Th
 is annual gathering brings together Native and non-Native community member
 s in a shared space of respect\, learning\, and connection. Guests will ex
 perience powerful performances by Native dancers\, singers\, and storytell
 ers\, explore traditional and contemporary artwork from talented Native ar
 tists and painters\, and enjoy cultural food and community engagement. The
  festival is a meaningful opportunity to uplift Native voices\, promote ar
 tistic expression\, and strengthen relationships across our broader commun
 ity. All are welcome to join us in honoring creativity\, culture\, and con
 nection.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/native-arts-festival-3/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emergence - Spring Through the Eyes of the Artists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T160000
UID:260401VSi5XFremk-AqmSmJL5JRg
DESCRIPTION:"Emergence" brings together the Artists of Fulton Crossing to 
 explore what Spring means to their creative lives. Spring is more than a s
 eason. It's a metaphor. It's renewal\, risk\, color\, thawing\, blooming\,
  awakening\, and sometimes even struggles. The public is invited to enjoy 
 this free Art exhibit and to take time to wander through the artists studi
 os and gallery spaces. Meet the artists at our opening reception March 21s
 t. Upcoming Art Workshops: March 21: Painting Easter Cookies. April 18: Ci
 gar Box Collage. May 16: Succulent Garden Centerpiece. Make treasures to b
 ring home. All ages welcome. Materials provided. E-mail Brenda at nanaspre
 ttypaper@outlook.com for preregistration and workshop info.
LOCATION:Fulton Crossing art gallery
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-
 the-artists/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
UID:260330CM9IsV-O3kWPfAQLSEL9ig
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
