BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:French Garden Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T160000
UID:2602281E8diqurgUiUVbDYfHXcNQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 9\, 2026\n\n12-4 p.m.  |  21 & Older Only\n\n
 $45 per person\n\nHeld just in time for Mother’s Day weekend\, Dry Creek
  Vineyard’s French Garden Market invites guests to step into the charm o
 f the French countryside with a festive outdoor celebration in the heart o
 f Dry Creek Valley. Visitors can browse a thoughtfully curated collection 
 of local artisans offering handcrafted treasures — from chic clothing an
 d jewelry to gourmet foods and home goods — perfect for spring gifting.\
 n\nGuests are invited to sip and savor the release of the winery’s newes
 t vintages of Petite Zin Rosé and Sauvignon Blanc while enjoying live mus
 ic by electric violinist Maya Victoria\, who brings a lively twist to mode
 rn pop favorites. The event also features Claudine\, the winery’s vintag
 e Citroën mobile bar and centerpiece of the wine garden\, along with deli
 cious bites from a local food pop-up. Attendees are encouraged to relax\, 
 linger\, and make a day of it.
LOCATION:Dry Creek Vineyard
URL:https://www.drycreekvineyard.com/product/french-garden-market-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T000000
UID:260227y0AzIQ_G00GKSsfZ1kaebw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Tasting Notes
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107935486?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
