DESCRIPTION:Join us at SVMA for an opening reception celebrating two new e
 xhibitions as part of our Year of Joy Through Art. John Paul Morabito: Dan
 cing in the Night features richly woven works that blend digital processes
  with handcraft\, transforming ritual materials into luminous tapestries t
 hat honor Queer life with color\, reverence\, and exuberance. Norma I. Qui
 ntana: Paradise of Memoryis a powerful portrait series drawing on itineran
 t photography traditions to connect personal and collective histories\, ce
 lebrating everyday lives as vital expressions of cultural identity. Saturd
 ay\, May 9\, 5 – 7 PM Event is free for SVMA members/$10 for non-members
 . Online registration is required by May 7 at 5 PM. Left: John Paul Morabi
 to\, Untitled \\(can’t stop dancing\\) 2024-25. Photographed by Field St
 udio Photography\, Courtesy of the Patricia Sweetow Gallery. Right: Norma 
 I. Quintana\, Oaxacan Women\, 2024\, Courtesy of the artist.
