BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Explore the Art and Science of Belgian Ales with Cuver Brewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T200000
UID:260425-5BDHS6DWUOjqCU1c0W3uQ
DESCRIPTION:**Headline: Beyond the Vine: Explore the Art of Belgian Brewin
 g with Cuver Brewing in Sonoma**\n\nJoin Sonoma Home Winemakers on **Thur
 sday\, May 14th**\, for a unique departure from our usual vine and wine fo
 cus. This evening we’re "brewing up" a special session featuring Hendrik
  Cuver (Brewmaster) and "Hoppy" Don Mills of Windsor’s **Cuver Brewing*
 *.\n\nFrom the science of Belgian yeast to the art of the hop and grain\, 
 learn how this family-run team combines "Old World" traditions with North 
 Bay innovation.\n\n**Where:** Sonoma Community Center\, Room 110\n\n**Whe
 n:** Doors 6:30 PM | Talk 7:00 PM\n\n**Cost:** Free\n\n**RSVP**: https://
 www.sonomahomewine.org/calendar\n\n**Note:** 21+ only\; Guests are encoura
 ged to bring a bottle of their homemade wine or a sampling of their homema
 de beer for the community tasting.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://www.sonomahomewine.org/calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T170000
UID:260424lkafvEF87ky6OXAHFVy5Sg
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa County Bike to Work and School Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T090000
UID:260422VYt3thtqDUuAcWHar397vQ
DESCRIPTION:Bike to Work & School Day celebrates the joy and many benefits
  of biking for transportation by bringing together the Napa County communi
 ty to swap their car trip to work\, school\, or wherever they need to go\,
  to a bicycle. Volunteers hosting energizer stations at schools and commun
 ity sites countywide will be handing out free snacks and swag and friendly
  encouragement to bicyclists in the morning of Bike to Work and School Day
 . All are invited to participate\, whether you're a seasoned bike commuter
  or this is your first time riding for transportation. Find more details\,
  a map of energizer stations and participating schools\, and pledge to rid
 e your bike for a chance to win prizes at bit.ly/BTWSD
LOCATION:Napa County
URL:https://napabike.org/bike-to-work-school-day/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parent Information Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T190000
UID:2604172NqCYcxe70iMwvhD1lSISg
DESCRIPTION:Are you exploring new options for your student’s education? 
 Come learn how our College Prep Program supports students in **grades 6
 –12** with a personalized\, student-centered approach in a **small\, s
 afe\, and supportive community**.\n\n✨ **What to Expect:**\n\n**Tour ou
 r campus** and see where students learn and grow\n\nLearn about our **co
 llege prep and career exploration programs** for both middle and high sch
 ool students\n\nDiscover our **intersession program**\, where students eng
 age in real-world learning experiences and college visits\n\nExplore our f
 ocus on **active\, engaged learning** and **high expectations** that h
 elp students thrive\n\nMeet a **current Quest Forward parent** and hear 
 their perspective\n\nGet answers to all your questions in a welcoming\, su
 pportive environment\n\nWhether you’re actively considering a change or 
 simply curious\, this is a great opportunity to see what makes Quest Forwa
 rd unique.\n\n👉 **All Santa Rosa families are welcome!**
LOCATION:Quest Forward High School
