BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Judgment of Paris-The Swirled Cup Documentary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
UID:260324ulh4DYYg30mTCOFFwdPwTQ
DESCRIPTION:The Swirled Cup explores the pivotal 1976 Judgment of Paris ta
 sting that reshaped the 8\,000-year-old wine industry in just one generati
 on.\n\nThis groundbreaking documentary will take you on a vibrant journey 
 into the culture of wine\, exploring how the combination of soil\, climate
 \, topography\, and human tradition-'terroir'-not only gives life to the v
 ines\, but also defines the personality of each wine.\n\nJoin Master Somme
 lier Andrea Immer Robinson for this 40-minute documentary\, panel discussi
 on with the wine makers\, and wine tasting of each of the wines discussed 
 in the documentary. Then\, head over to The Grove restaurant to enjoy a sp
 ecially curated French-inspired four-course prix fixe dinner experience wh
 ere you will have the opportunity to pair the wines from the documentary p
 erfectly with each and every course.
LOCATION:CIA at Copia
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/judgment-of-paris-the-s
 wirled-cup-documentary/18365019/2026-05-16T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fargo Brothers play ALA dinner-dance May 16 in Cloverdale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
UID:260324h-2iSQBgrkmQz50uozXk7Q
DESCRIPTION:The Fargo Brothers\, voted "Best Dance Band" by the Northbay M
 usic Awards in 2023\, 2024 and 2025\, play a rollicking dinner-dance fundr
 aiser in Cloverdale on Saturday\, May 16. Tickets are $50 per person and i
 nclude dinner\, wine and entertainment. The evening begins at 6 p.m. at th
 e Veterans Hall\, 205 W. First St. in Cloverdale. Tickets must be purchase
 d in advance by calling Melonie Delsid at (707) 953-5219 or emailing Delsi
 d1@comcast.net. Tickets will not be available at the door.\n\nThe event is
  slated to support the American Legion Auxiliary's Melanie Taylor\, a resi
 dent of Cloverdale and former President of Cloverdale ALA Unit 293\, who i
 s scheduled to take the office of the Auxiliary's National President in Ju
 ly 2028. While some of the National President's expenses will be reimburse
 d\, many are not\; thus Auxiliary Unit 293 is producing this event and wil
 l continue to support Taylor's campaign fundraising. Among Taylor's duties
  during her year as National President will be traveling to visit Units ac
 ross the nation\, and hosting a reception in Washington\, D.C.\, in 2029 t
 o honor the person elected as the 48th President of the United States.
LOCATION:Cloverdale Veterans Hall
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/fargo-brothers-play-ala
 -dinner-dance-may-16-in-cloverdale/18341985/2026-05-16T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
