BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Room in the Castle - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
UID:260426qboToEi2bky3FgU_WJp7fA
DESCRIPTION:A Room in the Castle is a feminist reimagining of William Shak
 espeare’s Hamlet\, written by prolific American playwright Lauren M. Gu
 nderson. The play shifts the perspective of the classic tragedy to focus e
 ntirely on the women of Elsinore: Ophelia\, Queen Gertrude\, and Ophelia
 ’s handmaid\, Anna.\n\nThe troubled\, grieving Prince of Denmark is neve
 r far from the thoughts of Ophelia\, a caretaker to Ophelia\, and the Quee
 n of Denmark. Playwright Lauren Gunderson does a masterful job re-imaginin
 g the women trapped by class\, circumstances\, expectations\, and desire w
 ithin the castle’s walls. Each\, in their own way\, follows the queen’
 s edict for women—to “obey\, agree\, assist”—until they absolutely
  do not. This play dances and duels with Hamlet\, foregrounding the women 
 in the play and re-imagining them with agency\, vitality\, and radical hea
 rts eager for a more hopeful ending.\n\nThe women of Hamlet have moments t
 hat are wholly their own. They own the stage—and our hearts.  ­— DC 
 TheaterArts\n\nFeaturing: Tatiana – Luisa Sermol / Ophelia – Marie Sad
 d / Gertrude – Leontyne Mbele Mbong\n\nDirected by Amy Kossow: "I have s
 een Hamlet so many times but here finally is a chance to stop and ask what
  the women are doing while all the men plot and scheme.  Lauren Gunderson
  gives Gertrude and Ophelia \\(along with a mysterious third woman\\) a wh
 ole play all to themselves\, and as the events of Hamlet unfold around the
 m\, these three create their own brilliant stories.\n\n- Sponsored in part
  by Melinda & Paul Pressler -\n\n-Theatre - Programmed by Aldo Billingslea
  and Amy Kossow -
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://the222.org/product/a-room-in-the-castle/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fifth Annual Call of the Wild Festival & Free Guided Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
UID:260425sX_L0Wq550m_dTxLgHyV5A
DESCRIPTION:The Fifth Annual Call of the Wild Festival is a fun-filled com
 munity celebration presented by Jack London Park Partners. It's also part 
 of the yearlong celebration of Jack London's 150th birthday.\n\nA free **F
 amily and Friends Hike**\, (normally $10 per person) will be offered at 10
  a.m.-1 p.m.  \n\nThe guided hike will pass through the canopy of redwoo
 ds and mixed evergreens on the way to London Lake\, with an option to cont
 inue to the majestic Ancient Redwood\, estimated to be between 1\,800-2\,0
 00 years old.  This is a moderate hike of approximately 3.5 miles round t
 rip with some elevation gain. Participants should wear sturdy shoes\, brin
 g plenty of water\, and snacks\, and dress in layers.  Dogs are not allow
 ed on backcountry trails.\n\nReservations for the Family and Friends Hike 
 are required and can be made at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/family-h
 ike-2026/.\n\nA full day of family-friendly activities\, plus tasty foods 
 and drinks are planned:\n\n11 a.m. and 1 p.m.          Guided tou
 rs to the Wolf House\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m.                Jack
  London Treasure Map art project with ArtEscape\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m.    
             Face painting with ArtEscape\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m. 
                Country musician Tommy Thomsen will perform l
 ive in the Winery ruins\, courtesy of Music in Place. \n\n11 a.m. - 3 p.m
 .                Beauty Ranch Bingo & The Adventure Quest Pa
 ssport\n\nPick up a Beauty Ranch Bingo card or an Adventure Quest Passport
  and let it guide you through Jack London’s inspiring history\, agricult
 ure\, and innovation. Complete a card or passport quest to receive a prize
 .\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Blacksmith demonstrat
 ion in front of the Distillery building.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.        
           Tractor-pulled hayrides around the Beauty Ranch.\n\n11 
 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Additional kid-friendly games
  and crafts in the Winery Ruins.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.            
       Tri Tip Trolley will serve savory favorites and comfort food cl
 assics\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Kona Ice.  Coo
 l off with a refreshing cup of tropical shaved ice in the spirit of Jack L
 ondon’s adventures in the South Seas.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.         
          Treat yourself to a cider with Tilted Shed Ciderworks.\n\
 n11:30 a.m.-12:30 p.m.    Storytelling in the House of Happy Walls Muse
 um.   Brandon Spars will share stories from “Tales of the Fish Patrol\
 ,” inspired by Jack London’s experiences as a teenager on the San Fran
 cisco Bay in the early 1890s.\n\nSpars is an educator\, author\, and accom
 plished storyteller who weaves together ancient history and narrative\, wi
 th four published books\, a TEDx talk\, and performances at renowned story
 telling festivals\, including the National Storytelling Festival.\n\n1 p.m
 .                                Guided tour
  of Jack London’s Beauty Ranch\n\nThe Call of the Wild Festival is suppo
 rted by the City of Sonoma with funding from the City’s Recreation and C
 ommunity Services Program.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/call-of-the-wild-festival-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T170000
UID:260424dPzRgMvjSE2TEKoUjNS84Q
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
