BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Private Screening of American Graffiti with 60’s Diner Dinner at
  Costeaux
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T210000
UID:260422atFx89vmPEa6GqCar-jETg
DESCRIPTION:Come dressed in your best greaser style and step back in time 
 for this throwback evening. Enjoy a 1960s‑inspired dinner at Costeaux 
 French Bakery—which has served as Healdsburg's Bakery for over 100 years
 . The dinner will take place from 5:30-6:45pm\, and will include classic b
 urgers and fries\, root beer floats\, and wine and beer. There will also b
 e vintage cars on display outside\, so you can truly travel back in time.
  \n\nAfter dinner\, head to Healdsburg's film hub\, True West Film Center
 \, for a private 7:15pm screening of George Lucas and Francis Ford Coppola
 's coming-of-age classic\, American Graffiti. Filmed in Petaluma\, this 19
 73 film perfectly encapsulates the sights\, sounds\, and spirit of 1960s A
 merica. Concessions will also be available for all attendees. \n\n**Our s
 incere gratitude to True West Film Center for making this experience possi
 ble.** \n\n100% of proceeds from this event go to Boys & Girls Clubs of So
 noma-Marin. These funds support us in providing after-school programs\, su
 mmer camps\, and essential resources for 11\,000 local youth—at Clubs fr
 om Geyserville to Petaluma. \n\n**Ticket sales for this event are live an
 d close on Sunday\, April 26th at 6pm.**
LOCATION:Costeaux French Bakery
URL:https://hbginbloom2026.ggo.bid/n/package/15104468
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Candidates Night 2nd Dist. Supervisor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T193000
UID:2604207Kdevv2RpUW5aSHibps4XQ
DESCRIPTION:**Penngrove Cares**\n\n**INVITES PUBLIC TO 2nd District Candi
 date Night**\n\n**Tuesday\, May 19\, 2026\, at 6:00 pm**\n\n**At Penngrove
  Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward Ave.\, Penngrove\, CA**\n\n To enable
  voters to hear the candidates and question them about important issues be
 fore the June 2 Primary election.\n\n Penngrove Cares will sponsor a 2nd 
 District candidates forum on **Tuesday\, May 19\, 2026\,** at 6:00 pm at 
 Penngrove Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward Ave.\, Penngrove. \n\n Cand
 idates for the 2nd District Supervisor include John King\, Sylvia Lemus\,
  Shelina Moreda\, and Joanna Paun.\n\n The event format consists of the c
 andidates making timed opening and closing statements and answering questi
 ons submitted by the Penngrove community and the audience. Note: the event
  will be in-person only.\n\n District 2 includes the cities of Petaluma 
 and Cotati and a portion of Rohnert Park\, as well as the unincorporated c
 ommunities of Penngrove\, Two Rock\, Bloomfield\, and a portion of the uni
 ncorporated community south of Sebastopol.\n\n The event is organized by 
 Penngrove Cares\, *a community forum* *for issues affecting the Penngrov
 e area\;* and by Penngrove Downtown Merchants.\n\n Ballot drop‐off locat
 ions open May 5\, with in-person polls open on June 2. For information\, p
 lease visit: **https://caearlyvoting.sos.ca.gov/**\n\n Further informati
 on is available from penngrovecares@sonic.net or https://PenngroveCares.or
 g.\n\nFacebook – Penngrove Cares: https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?i
 d=61578317972832
LOCATION:Penngrove Clubhouse
URL:https://www.penngrovecares.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
