BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pond Farm Artist in Residence 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T000000
UID:260424bghSRQCl4EK7khJSkBC8Jw
DESCRIPTION:Pond Farm Pottery is the former home and studio of renowned ma
 ster potter\, artist\, and educator\, Marguerite Wildenhain\, and a new Na
 tional Historic Landmark. Pond Farm is located above Armstrong Redwoods\, 
 in beautiful Guerneville\, California. Spend your time in a private cabin 
 at Pond Farm Pottery. Breathtaking inspirational views. Miles and miles of
  hiking. 5 minute drive to Armstrong Redwoods\; 15 minute drive to downtow
 n Guerneville for shopping/art/restaurants/wine tasting\; 30 minutes to th
 e Sonoma Coast\; and approximately 1 hr 45 minutes to San Francisco. Pond 
 Farm Pottery offers an Artist-in-Residence \\(AiR\\) program funded by  Ar
 ts in California Parks \, a program of CA State Parks\, Parks California\,
  and California Arts Council.  Click here for more information about AiR a
 t Pond Farm . Visit Pond Farm by registering for a docent-led tour on our 
  events page  Fill out the application here
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/pond-farm-artist-in-residence-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Acoustic Sunsets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T200000
UID:260416AzVt3MP5fEKwEJ5xdRvKAw
DESCRIPTION:*Acoustic Sunsets* returns for its third season!  From **Ma
 y 6 through September 16\\***\, the Garden extends its hours Wednesday eve
 nings until **8:00 pm**. Each evening features live music by Bay Area mus
 icians in our outdoor amphitheater from **5:30–7:30 pm**. Guests are i
 nvited to bring picnics and well-behaved dogs on leash\, enjoy wine tastin
 gs with local vintners\, and unwind in the Garden’s beautiful\, natural 
 setting. New this year! Monthly ***Noche Latina*** nights celebrating La
 tin music and culture in conjunction with the special exhibition ***Spiri
 t Guides: Fantastical Creatures from the Workshop of Jacobo and María Án
 geles***.\n\nFree for Sonoma Botanical Garden members and included in gene
 ral admission for non-members. This is a drop-in program and tickets are s
 old at check-in\, no advance registration is required.\n\n\\*No concerts J
 une 10 or July 1
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/acoustic-sunsets/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
