BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T170000
UID:2604244YXXTAdj_0eECvh_EUgdHA
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ICSTESH
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T170000
UID:2604229LF4_dQG60WHmhP9LaRzwQ
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the International Conference on Societal Transforma
 tion through Engineering\, Education\, Social Science\, and Humanities (IC
 STESH 2026)\, taking place on May 21 & 22\, 2026\, in the dynamic and rapi
 dly developing city of Astana\, Kazakhstan. Organized by IFERP Academy\, t
 his conference marks a transformative global platform where innovative min
 ds\, researchers\, educators\, policymakers\, and industry leaders converg
 e to inspire real-world impact.\n\nWith the theme “Bridging Innovation a
 nd Inclusion: Empowering Global Societal Transformation for a Sustainable 
 Future\,” ICSTESH 2026 aims to spark groundbreaking ideas\, foster cross
 -disciplinary collaboration\, and empower communities through knowledge-dr
 iven solutions. We warmly invite you to be part of this enriching experien
 ce as we collectively shape a future anchored in sustainability\, inclusiv
 ity\, and global progress.
LOCATION:Copperfield's Books- Petaluma
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/icstesh/18631089/2026-0
 5-21T09
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
