BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friday Night Comedy - Terrell "Big T" Butler - Downtown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T220000
UID:260404iG2SHYUAQEqWE-uqFMOs8Q
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TAB
 LES NOW AVAILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own pr
 ivate call button to summon service\, and your first round of drinks (or a
  bottle of wine) for only $95!\n\nEvery Friday night hilarious comedians f
 rom The Bay Area and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around a
 fter for late-night karaoke! Fresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThis We
 ek: Jon Lehre (host) Jon Alcabes Headliner: Terrell 'Big T' Butler\n\nTerr
 ell Butler is originally from Oakland California. Affectionally referred t
 o by his nickname Big-T\, he has always been the comedian of his social ci
 rcle. Taking the stage for the first time in 2007 as a stand up comic\, he
  hit the ground running. He has quickly earned respect at the premier come
 dy clubs across Northern and Southern California as a feature performer.\n
 \nTerrell is a graduate of Academy Of Art University\, with a degree in Co
 m- munication and Media Technology. He has hosted several Live Stream TV S
 hows\, Produced two radio shows “The Bridge” & “The Rise N’ Grind 
 Show”. He also worked as the Program Director for Urban Knight Radio at 
 AAU.\n\nBig-T is the Winner of the 2016 Rooster T. Feathers Comedy Competi
 tion\, in Sunnyvale CA. As a stand up comedian\, Big-T draws his comedy fr
 om life ex- perience. Ranging from The colorful characters in his family\,
  his life as an Oak- land youth\, and his years as a bouncer in Bay Area n
 ightclubs & gentlemens clubs. Comedy has awakened a new spirit in the 6 fo
 ot 3\, 315 pound\, devilishly Handsome\, Big-T. Terrell credits his influe
 nce in stand up to legends like Eddie Murphy\, Richard Pryor\, and Robert 
 Townsand. A spirit that has inspired him to this day.\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / 
 Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** fo
 r all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/friday-night-comedy-terrell-big-t-butler-
 downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1984347749536?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emergence - Spring Through the Eyes of the Artists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T160000
UID:260401EeqYawsHz0uWwUJnMOzToA
DESCRIPTION:"Emergence" brings together the Artists of Fulton Crossing to 
 explore what Spring means to their creative lives. Spring is more than a s
 eason. It's a metaphor. It's renewal\, risk\, color\, thawing\, blooming\,
  awakening\, and sometimes even struggles. The public is invited to enjoy 
 this free Art exhibit and to take time to wander through the artists studi
 os and gallery spaces. Meet the artists at our opening reception March 21s
 t. Upcoming Art Workshops: March 21: Painting Easter Cookies. April 18: Ci
 gar Box Collage. May 16: Succulent Garden Centerpiece. Make treasures to b
 ring home. All ages welcome. Materials provided. E-mail Brenda at nanaspre
 ttypaper@outlook.com for preregistration and workshop info.
LOCATION:Fulton Crossing art gallery
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-
 the-artists/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T170000
UID:260330uZeXGUngd0yvJLFb0bELKQ
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonalice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T000000
UID:260327xlKVp3W2yECzR8aDcxcnFg
DESCRIPTION:Moonalice is a psychedelic\, roots-rock band of seasoned music
 ians mixing a variety of genres with extended musical improvisations that 
 evoke a sense of adventure and exploration. Everyone is a part of the expe
 rience and the music inspires dancing and other acts of self expression. E
 very show has an original art poster created by a well-known artist memori
 alizing that event and given to all attendees…each poster has its own Mo
 onalice legend. All concerts are broadcasted live in HD and available in a
 rchive shortly after their set.\n\nMoonalice plays mostly original materia
 l mixed with several covers\, and during their extended freeform jams the 
 band moves as one\, drawing from many musical genres honed from years of e
 xperience playing with various major acts. Their single "It's 4:20 Somewhe
 re" has been downloaded over 6 million times. Just released: 420 Gathering
  of the Tribe by Jay Blakesberg and Alex Fischer – a short film about th
 e Moonalice posters and poster artists: http://www.moonalice.com/song/its-
 420-somewhere. Social media: nearly 424\,000 on Facebook & over 67\,000 on
  Twitter. Their extensive tour schedule and videos of every Moonalice show
  can be seen at moonalice.com and every show poster with legends can be vi
 ewed at moonaliceposters.com.\n\nBand\n\nDylan Chambers: Vocals\, Cowbell 
 \\(Midnight Transit\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nLester Chambers: Voc
 als\, Harmonica \\(Chambers Brothers\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nJas
 on Crosby: Keyboards \\(Phil Lesh\, Terrapin Family Band\, Jenny Lewis\, J
 ohn McLaughlin\, Robert Randolph\, Blind Boys of Alabama\, Susan Tedeschi\
 \)\n\nRoger McNamee: Rhythm Guitar\, Vocals\, Bass. \\(Guff\, The Engineer
 s\, Random Axes\, Flying Other Brothers\\)\n\nJohn Molo: Drums\, Vocals. \
 \(Bruce Hornsby & The Range\, John Fogerty\, Phil Lesh & Friends\, The Oth
 er Ones\, David Nelson Band\\).\n\nPete Sears: Bass\, Keyboards\, Guitar\,
  Vocals \\(Sam Gopal Dream\, Rod Stewart\, Jefferson Starship\, Jerry Garc
 ia\, Hot Tuna\, John Lee Hooker\, David Nelson Band\, Phil Lesh & Friends\
 \).\n\nBarry Sless: Lead Guitar\, Pedal Steel Guitar\, Bass. \\(Phil Lesh 
 & Friends\, David Nelson Band\, Kingfish\, Cowboy Jazz\\).\n\nChloe Tietje
 n: Vocals \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nErika Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\
 )\n\nRachel Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nFun facts\n\nMoona
 lice’s first show was in May\, 2007.\n\nMoonalice’s single\, “It’s
  4:20 Somewhere” has been downloaded more than 5 million times.\n\nMoona
 lice invented the Twittercast concert\, broadcasting links in near real ti
 me for live concerts and at random times for past shows. The band has done
  103 Twittercast concerts.\n\nMoonalice is the first band to Mooncast live
  video of all of its concerts. Moonalice has broadcast nearly ever concert
  since 2010\, the first band to operate a satellite-based broadcast system
  that enables High Definition live video to smartphones and iPads WITHOUT 
 an app!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1038243872?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
