UID:260424CYX_UNW8SU6SbYK7aVw4aQ
DESCRIPTION:Pond Farm Pottery is the former home and studio of renowned ma
 ster potter\, artist\, and educator\, Marguerite Wildenhain\, and a new Na
 tional Historic Landmark. Pond Farm is located above Armstrong Redwoods\, 
 in beautiful Guerneville\, California. Spend your time in a private cabin 
 at Pond Farm Pottery. Breathtaking inspirational views. Miles and miles of
  hiking. 5 minute drive to Armstrong Redwoods\; 15 minute drive to downtow
 n Guerneville for shopping/art/restaurants/wine tasting\; 30 minutes to th
 e Sonoma Coast\; and approximately 1 hr 45 minutes to San Francisco. Pond 
 Farm Pottery offers an Artist-in-Residence \\(AiR\\) program funded by  Ar
 ts in California Parks \, a program of CA State Parks\, Parks California\,
  and California Arts Council.  Click here for more information about AiR a
 t Pond Farm . Visit Pond Farm by registering for a docent-led tour on our 
  events page  Fill out the application here
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/pond-farm-artist-in-residence-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
